<BaseLayout lang="en" title="VKU Zug preparation – documents and your first class" description="What should you bring to the Zug VKU? Prepare for your first class, find the entrance and check how the rules change for a course starting in 2027." >
 <header class="page-top"><div class="wrap"><p class="overline">DriveLab · Zug</p><h1>VKU Zug – get ready for your first class</h1><p>Know which documents to bring and how to find the door on Industriestrasse before you set off.</p></div></header>

 <section class="plan-section wrap split-plan"><div><h2>What should I bring?</h2><ul class="checklist">
 <li>For a 2026 course, bring your valid Swiss learner’s permit. Keep the booking confirmation with all dates handy.</li>
 <li>Charge your phone so you can open the digital materials in class. Writing supplies and learning materials are provided.</li>
 <li>Save every session with its finishing time. Check your return journey separately, especially after an evening class. Drinks and fruit are included.</li></ul>
 </div><figure><img src="/images/eingang-drivelab.webp" width="1039" height="780" alt="Classroom entrance with DriveLab lettering on the window" class="rounded-lg w-full" /><figcaption>Entrance on Industriestrasse. DriveLab photograph from 2023.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section class="plan-section wrap"><h2>What you will practise</h2><p>Imagine turning right near Zug station. A cyclist is alongside you and someone is waiting at a crossing. In class you discuss where to look first, which road users may cross your path and how much space to leave. Then consider how rain or darkness changes the same decision.</p>
 <h3>After the last session</h3><p>The provider records completion digitally once you have attended every session. If you miss a session, contact DriveLab to arrange the outstanding part.</p>
 <h3>Courses starting in January 2027</h3><p>Under the new training rules you complete the VKU before the basic theory test. The eight hours are spread over four separate days. Have your FABER PIN ready. If you already passed the theory test in 2026, you still need proof of attendance before the practical test.</p>
 <div class="inline-links"><a href="https://www.astra.admin.ch/de/anderungen-vom-19-dezember-2025">Federal Roads Office rules</a><a href="/en/kursinhalt">Explore the four course topics</a></div>
 <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="action" href="/en/course-dates">Find a course group →</a></p></section>
</BaseLayout>
